    {
      "_id": "LicLY5imaFaETCVI",
      "name": "Mesh Inserts",
      "type": "physicalTech",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>This network of implants is mandatory for people who want to use augmented reality and link wirelessly to the mesh. The various components include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cranial Computer: This host serves as the hub for your personal area network and is home to your muse. It manages your augmented reality input and processes XP data, enabling you to share your sensorium with others in real-time. It is loaded with basic apps and provides all the functions you would expect from a mobile device: file storage, search engine, media player, mesh browser, address book, e-mail, messaging, and so forth.</li>\n<li>Medical/Diagnostic Sensors: This array monitors your health, including heart rate, respiration, blood pressure, temperature, neural activity, ware status, and more. In synthmorphs, this system monitors system reports and error logs, heat, stress faults, and similar hardware statuses.</li>\n<li>Radio Transceiver: This connects your headware with other mesh devices within range (5 km urban areas/50 km open areas).</li>\n<li>You can access any of these functions simply by thinking.</li>\n</ul>",
        "reference": "Eclipse Phase Second Edition p. 316",
        "complexity": "minor",
        "restricted": false,
